**How to implement.** The composition root is closed and the whole tree proves 001 §V (001 §V 'Done when'; 001 §R; 001 §F, §G, §O; the Close brief; .spec-md §0, §3.9, §3.10, §3.12, §9 'Done when'; AGENTS.md: a comment says why in one to three lines; drive by id and wait for deterministic conditions). When this step starts, `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs` and `AppContext.create` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`) already compose everything 001 asks of the root, each wired by the step that introduced it: the SQLite library over the configured `DataLocations` (`Program.fs:Startup`, `AppConfig.loadWorkbenchSettings`, steps 83, 88, 89), the catalogue import on every start (step 100), the start screen behind Main and Inverse (steps 180, 191, 232), the kit window with the flow-strip steps of its mode (steps 189, 242, 323, 414-419, 490-492) and the Data locations window behind the Launcher's footer link (step 195). This step changes no code in those two files: it rewrites their stale docs, updates AGENTS.md, and proves the composition end to end. (1) Docs, each citing spec 0050 Close. `Program.fs`: the first paragraph of the file doc (`Program.fs:1-6`, spec 0038's launcher narrative) becomes at most four lines: the root reads the settings and the locations once (`Startup`), composes `AppContext.create` over them, and shows `LauncherWindow`, whose Main and Inverse open `KitStartWindow` and whose footer opens `DataLocationsWindow`; a chosen kit opens the constructor window of its mode (`KitConstructorWindows.showConstructorIn`), which runs the kit window. The file doc's second paragraph (`Program.fs:8-12`, the FuncUI clone) is unchanged. The docs of `Startup.workbenchSettings` and `Startup.context` (`Program.fs:37-47` and `:50-58` today, edited by steps 83 and 88) become one to three lines each: the settings and `DataLocations` that `appsettings.json` gives, read once; and the one app scope `AppContext.create` answers over them, an open failure shown by the launcher (step 88). `AppContext.fs`: its file doc (`AppContext.fs:1-9`, spec 0038's in-memory narrative) becomes one to three lines: the one app scope, composed at the root over the configured locations (the SQLite library stores and the catalogue import of every start) and injected into the launcher, the start screen and every window. Any other doc in the two files that still says in-memory store, re-seed, experiment collection, scene store or a `STORE_XDUO_*` seam this spec deleted is cut to the words that stay true. (2) `AGENTS.md`, wherever this spec changed a fact it states; nothing else in the file changes. (a) `## Build & test`: the sentence `No test, fixture or kit lives under Documents; test kits and databases go under the test run's output directory.` (`AGENTS.md:60-61`) becomes: no test, fixture, kit or database lives under `Documents`, `%APPDATA%` or `%LOCALAPPDATA%`; `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`' own `appsettings.json` (step 82) and `TestAppScope` (`testLocations`, `fileLocations`) put every location, the SQLite library (`:memory:` or a file) included, under the test run's output directory, and the committed kits under `data/` are opened read-only (spec 0050 §3.9, §3.12). (b) `## Project layout` (`AGENTS.md:142-159`), in the block's column layout: `OpticalConstructor.Domain`'s note `project model` becomes `library entries, kits, setups, experiments, studies, planner`; `OpticalConstructor.Storage`'s note `project files, JSON (de)serialization, schema validation, export` becomes `kit folders, entry and catalogue files, canonical JSON, schema validation, SQLite library proxies, export`; and four lines are added: `BerremanTestSupport/` after `BerremanTests/` (shared test ground truth: crystal samples, designs, the committed-kit locator), `Catalogue/Builtin/` first under `OpticalConstructor/` (the shipped built-in library catalogue, as entry files), `OpticalConstructor.Database` after `OpticalConstructor.Storage` (the C# EF Core library model: SQLite, `EnsureCreated` plus a schema stamp) and `data/` after `Elevation/` (the committed reference experiment kits, read-only to tests). (c) `## Gotchas`, directly after 'The Main scene's Library is LIVE' (as steps 58 and 100 left it), three bullets of at most six lines each. **The library is data, not code** (spec 0050 S1-S3): every material, sample, source, polarizer, detector, item model and category is a versioned entry file (`<name>.material-json` and so on: canonical JSON with its SHA-256, `LibraryEntryEnvelope`) held in the SQLite library database (`library.db`, the `OpticalConstructorSqlite` connection string; EF Core `EnsureCreated` plus a schema stamp, never a migration); the built-ins ship as `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/Catalogue/Builtin/`, imported with every registered catalogue folder on every start by manifest hash (`CatalogueImportContext.importOnStart`); code names a built-in only by its frozen GUID (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`, `ItemModelIds`) and holds no seed value; a library of another schema is `LibrarySchemaMismatchErr`, which the Launcher remedies with Recreate library from catalogues. **Everything else lives in a kit folder** (`Kit.fs`, `KitOpening.fs`, spec 0050 S4-S12): a folder holding `.kit-json`, its root flat (`<label>.item-json`, `<name>.setup-json`, `<name>.experiment-json`, `<study>.study-json`, append-only `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json`) with three subfolders: `library/` (a snapshot of every library version the kit uses, so it opens on any machine), `data/` (lab files the app only reads, referenced by relative path and SHA-256) and `.oc/` (the lock and the Planner's derived cache, never sent); logic reaches it only through `KitProxy` (`KitProxy.create (folder : KitFolder)`) in a `KitContext`; every write is atomic (`*.tmp`, then replace), a read-only open writes nothing, and a file of another schema version is `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`. **Main and Inverse open the kit start screen** (`KitStartView.fs`, `KitStartWindow.fs`, spec 0050 S5-S6): New kit… (an empty folder is initialised, a folder with files keeps them), Open kit…, Open kit from zip… and the history (`KitHistoryProxy` in the per-user preferences, at most `KitHistoryLimit`, starred first); a chosen kit opens the constructor of that mode, one window per kit, titled by the kit and its folder; Materials and Library need no kit; the Launcher's footer link opens Data locations, every `DataLocations` path, each overridable in `appsettings.json`. (d) 'Main ribbon' (as step 328 left it) gains one sentence: the kit window's left flow strip (`FlowStripView.fs`, `ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf`) reaches Items, Setups and Experiments, the last being this bay, in both constructors, and Data, Unknowns, Plan, Fit, Results and Publish in the Inverse one alone. (3) Tests, in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs`, whose module doc gains one to three lines citing spec 0050 Close naming the two proofs below. Each new fact runs on `HeadlessSession.run`, finds a control by its `Name` or `AutomationId`, presses a box at its centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:69` (`clickOn`) does, observes the windows a click opens through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent` as `LauncherTests.fs:58` (`clickAndObserve`) does, waits only through `Dispatcher.UIThread.RunJobs`, never a sleep, and closes every window it opened, so no `WindowRegistry` key outlives it. With trait `ui-smoke`: (a) `acceptance: the composed app goes from the Launcher through the start screen to a kit under the test output and shows every flow-strip step of its mode`: over `locations = TestAppScope.fileLocations (FolderName "WireUiFinalCompositionTests")` (step 88: a SQLite library file under the test output, the build-copied `Catalogue/Builtin` as the shipped catalogue), `AppContext.create locations WorkbenchSettings.defaults` answers `Ok ctx`, composed as `Program.fs:Startup` composes the app, an `Error` failing the fact with its `describe`; the file `LibraryDatabase.tryFileOf locations.libraryConnection` names exists and `ctx.materials.tryGetMaterial MaterialIds.silicon` answers Silicon, so the start-up import ran into the database. With `kit = TestAppScope.freshKitFolder (FolderName "WireUiFinalCompositionTests")` (step 152), a shown `LauncherWindow(locations, WorkbenchSettings.defaults, Ok ctx, fun _ -> TestAppScope.kitPickerOf kit)` (steps 89, 154): raising `Click` on `openInverseButton` opens exactly one `KitStartWindow`, titled `Open a kit — Inverse`; pressing its `newKitButton` opens exactly one `InverseConstructorWindow`, closes the start screen, leaves `.kit-json` and `.oc/lock` in `kit` and makes `kit` the first entry of `ctx.kitHistory.readHistory ()`; the window's title ends with ` — Optical Constructor — Inverse`; its flow strip holds one box per step of `ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf InverseConstructor`, and pressing each, in order, shows its surface: `itemsPanel` (Items), `tableElementCanvas` (Setups), the Experiments bay's pane `ConstructorUiId.ribbonPane` of its key (Experiments), `dataStepPanel` (Data), `studyUnknownsPanel` (Unknowns), `planPanel` (Plan), `studyFitPanel` (Fit), `studyResultsPanel` (Results) and `studyPublishPanel` (Publish) (steps 242, 323, 414-418, 490); pressing `kitCloseButton` closes the window and leaves no `.oc/lock` in `kit`. Raising `Click` on `openMainButton` then opens exactly one `KitStartWindow` titled `Open a kit — Main`; pressing its `openKitButton` opens exactly one `MainConstructorWindow` over the same kit, whose flow strip holds `flowItemsStep`, `flowSetupsStep` and `flowExperimentsStep` and none of `flowDataStep`, `flowUnknownsStep`, `flowPlanStep`, `flowFitStep`, `flowResultsStep` and `flowPublishStep` (`stepsOf ForwardConstructor`), each of the three showing its surface when pressed; `kitCloseButton` closes it and leaves no `.oc/lock`. Raising `Click` on `launcherDataLocationsLink` opens exactly one `DataLocationsWindow`, whose `dataLocationPathText LibraryDatabaseLocation` reads the library file's full path and whose `dataLocationPathText KitsLocation` reads `locations.kitsFolder`'s text (steps 192, 193); it and the launcher are then closed. (b) `acceptance: the committed optics-mueller kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing` and (c) `acceptance: the committed absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing`, over `OpticsMuellerKit` and `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyKit` through one private function of the class: `TestAppScope.openCommittedReadOnly (FolderName "WireUiFinalCompositionTests") kit` (step 493: a start screen sending `OpenKitReadOnly` of the committed folder, against an empty library) answers the context, the Inverse window model and the recording; the model is mounted as `KitWindowTests` mounts its screens (step 312: `kitWindowView` over the model, dispatching through `updateTableAndElementRotation`, its shell `KitWindowShell.inert`) and shown; `kitCaptionText` contains ` (read-only)` (step 184); pressing each box of `ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf InverseConstructor` shows the surface (a) names; then the window is closed, the kit is closed as `KitAcceptanceTests` closes it, and `TestAppScope.assertCommittedUnchanged` of the kit and the recording holds, so nothing was written under `data/`. The class's earlier facts keep their names and assertions. (4) The whole-tree proof (001 §V), by the gates this step runs whole: AT-1 and AT-2, the two committed kits equal to their builds and their read-only runs under kit-acceptance (`KitAcceptanceTests`, steps 421-440); the Planner's §M facts (`MeasurementPlannerTests`, steps 475, 481) and BerremanTests' unchanged numbers under unit-tests; the library in the database and the kit's files in its folder under (3)(a); zero warnings from our code and an empty `Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json` under build, elevation and elevation-full. The 001 §R removals are confirmed by `git grep -n -i -F "ocproj" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -F -e SceneProxy -e ExperimentCollectionProxy -e recent.json -e seedAll -e TestDbContext -e SolverHandoffView -e MuellerDataSet -e MuellerDataProxy -e Data/MuellerMatrix -e experimentRegex -e measuredElementOf -- Berreman/`, each finding nothing: the steps that removed them (S1.6, S2.1, steps 152, 161, 169, 254, 270, 330-331 and 416) deleted every mention, and the section invariants have held each name out since. No retry, sleep, timer, product seam or project-file comment is added.

**Acceptance.** After the root is closed, `Program.fs` and `AppContext.create` MUST compose the SQLite library over `DataLocations`, the catalogue import of every start, the start screen behind Main and Inverse, the kit window with its mode's flow-strip steps and the Data locations window, and their docs MUST say so; AGENTS.md MUST state the library database, kit folders and their layout, the start screen, the flow strip and the test locations; the composed app MUST go from the Launcher through the start screen to a kit under the test output and show every flow-strip step of each mode, and each committed kit MUST open read-only from the start screen and leave `data/` unchanged; `git grep -n -i -F "ocproj" -- Berreman/` and `git grep -n -F -e SceneProxy -e ExperimentCollectionProxy -e recent.json -e seedAll -e TestDbContext -e SolverHandoffView -e MuellerDataSet -e MuellerDataProxy -e Data/MuellerMatrix -e experimentRegex -e measuredElementOf -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; build MUST pass with zero warnings from our code; elevation and elevation-full MUST pass with `Elevation/elevation-known-findings.json` listing no finding; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass whole; ui-smoke MUST pass whole, including `acceptance: the composed app goes from the Launcher through the start screen to a kit under the test output and shows every flow-strip step of its mode`, `acceptance: the committed optics-mueller kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing` and `acceptance: the committed absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit opens read-only from the start screen, shows every flow-strip step and writes nothing`, the count rising by 3; ui-tests MUST pass whole; unit-tests MUST pass whole with BerremanTests' numbers unchanged; kit-acceptance MUST pass whole; and the twenty-one s47 invariants MUST pass.
